  "summary": "Remove every Xingcheng parameter-count lower bound while retaining the 20B total upper bound and independent capability gates.",
  "changes": [
    {
      "table": "articles",
      "key": { "provision_id": "B135" },
      "field": "rule",
      "proposed": "XINGCHENG-MODEL-SCALE:every publishable Xingcheng model configuration has no total_parameter_count lower bound and has a 20B inclusive total upper bound;any scale at or below 20B may be used when its actual capability,performance and resource conditions are satisfied;FULL-CAPABILITY-BASELINE:a full-capability baseline has no parameter-count lower bound;PARAMETER-COUNT-SEMANTICS:parameter count establishes only the upper scale and resource boundary and never proves maturity,quality or capability;all capability,quality,compatibility,resource and rollback gates remain independently mandatory;OWNER:XINGCHENG may adapt architecture,density,MoE activation and internal tiering below the 20B upper bound and within current Codex authority,permission and resource limits."
